            <ArticleTitle>Atrophoderma Vermiculatum in a Father and Son.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>355-356</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 10 year old boy and his father presented with atrophoderma vermiculatum. The son had multiple pits preceded by horny papules since 5 years of age while the father 40 year old had honey comb atrophy on both cheeks. The histopathology of skin lesions revealed non-specific peri-follicular inflammation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
